# Defense in depth, not the mechanism.
#
# The evaluator id is a hash over file contents — rubric.yaml, the judge prompt
# template, verdict.schema.json. A Windows checkout with CRLF and a Linux CI
# checkout with LF would hash to different evaluator ids for identical content,
# so `verify` would fail on line endings and report it as evaluator drift.
#
# This setting only governs files that arrive through a checkout of this repo.
# The authority is normalizeBlob() in src/identity.ts, which every blob passes
# through before hashing. That covers pasted rubrics, a contributor with a
# mangled core.autocrlf, and files that reach disk by any other route.
* text=auto eol=lf
